# Shell Non-Overlap (HARD)

Authority: `unity/Assets/Plans/SHELL_NON_OVERLAP_RULE.md`

## Law

No two shell pieces may occupy the same space. Tiles end where others begin. Overlap / nesting is a generator bug.

## Must

- Assemble **floor-stack bottom-up** (storey 0→N), not full-height annex volumes.
- Same-floor slabs: XZ interiors disjoint (touching plane OK).
- Pieces: AABB ⊆ owning slab (inward walls).
- Party bay → emit nothing; step bay → wall + AtticWindow only.
- Door only on floor 0; bay cell ≤1 wall + ≤1 opening.
- Chimney bottom flush on primary top roof.
- After assemble: `ShellOverlapGuard.Validate` must pass.

## Forbidden

- Double walls/windows on height-step seams
- Floating chimneys
- Roof/foundation overshoot into neighbor slab
- Standard Window on attic/step faces

Do not merge shell grammar that fails the guard or weakens this rule.
